# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-4 and NOT-9: the empty log takes the whole screen, and gives every
# pixel of it back.
# A single leg, and it has to be one. The key that opens the log reaches
# the program in a seam-off run, where the adventuring bar answers an
# unknown letter by stepping its own highlight, so from that moment the
# two runs differ on the bar row whatever the give-back does, and what a
# pair would measure is the highlight (#234).
# So the give-back is stated directly and more strongly: the frame after
# the log closes is the same screen as the frame before it opened.
# Driven on the shorter boot (`--code-wheel-answered`, #291).

about the log takes the whole screen and gives every pixel of it back
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel

# No `document` line, and that is #290 rather than an omission: no seam in
# this build is gated now. rdr-bar.leg is the same shape.
code-wheel-answered
seam journal
until 220000000
every 25

# Slot A, the log, and out by Escape. **The frame the way out lands on is
# chosen, not arbitrary** (#325): a keystroke reaches the program at one
# of two points, its poll or its blocking read, and which one is a matter
# of where its key loop stood when the frame began. On this boot Escape at
# 10,400 to 10,410 lands at the poll and 10,411 at the read - measured
# with the read point logging its arrivals - and the read is where the
# give-back's keystroke was once lost behind the read's own answer. Driven
# with that answer posted behind the space again, the `equal` below
# reports `910 pixels differ, box 1,192,311,198`: the bar row, and nothing
# but it, from the give-back to the end of the run.
key L@7550
key A@7800
key N@9600
key Escape@10411

# The log up, holding still, with nothing pressed. Measured: one hash from
# 9,725 to 10,411.
same 9800-10375

# The screen before the log, back again after it: every pixel, the bar row
# included, from 10,650 to the end of the run.
equal 9600 10800
